Stops `colcon build` from descending into legacy/.

legacy/ws/src/control/ is a dead ROS2 python package (an AGV diff-drive
teleop/setpoint controller from an earlier project, maintainer cameron)
kept only for reference. Without this marker colcon discovers it as a
6th workspace package named "control" and builds it on every plain
`colcon build` -- see GitHub issue #22, where a fresh-arm build reported
"Starting >>> control" for a package that isn't in src/ at all, which is
exactly as confusing as it sounds.

Do not delete this file. If you ever need to build something in here,
move it into src/ rather than removing the marker.
